#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the managed workflows client package, authenticate to IBM Quantum "
"Platform, and verify your setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install {#install}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites {#prerequisites}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Managed workflows enabled on your [IBM Quantum&reg; Platform "
"instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances). Contact your "
"administrator to enable it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An API key and the CRN of your instance. See [Find your access "
"credentials](/guides/save-credentials#find-credentials).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Python 3.10 or later, in an active virtual environment. See [Install "
"Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit#local) for how to set up an environment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quick start with AI skills {#quick-start-with-ai-skills}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use the AI skills in the [Qiskit Function templates "
"repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates) "
"to help you install `qiskit-ibm-catalog`, package your existing local code, "
"and deploy it as a managed workflow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the client package {#install-the-client-package}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the `qiskit-ibm-catalog` package:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This command also installs `qiskit-serverless`, `qiskit`, and `qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime` as dependencies. You do not need to install `qiskit-serverless` "
"separately. The examples in these guides require `qiskit-ibm-catalog` 0.22.0"
" or later, which installs `qiskit-serverless` 0.38 and `qiskit-ibm-runtime` "
"0.51.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You use two of these packages directly, in different places:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`qiskit-ibm-catalog` is the client that you use on your local computer to "
"upload workflows, run them, and get their results.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`qiskit-serverless` runs inside your workflow code. It provides helpers such"
" as `get_arguments()`, `update_status()`, and `save_result()`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Update the client package {#update-the-client-package}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because managed workflows is in beta, the client package changes often. To "
"check which version you have, run the following command:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Or, in Python:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To update to the latest version, run the following command:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the new version of `qiskit-ibm-catalog` requires a newer version of "
"`qiskit-serverless`, this command also updates `qiskit-serverless`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Authenticate {#authenticate}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"danger\" title=\"Protect your API key\">\n"
"Do not include your API key in your workflow code, in scripts, or in notebook files. A running workflow uses the credentials and instance that you used to call `run()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The managed workflows client uses the same credentials as `qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime`. If you already saved an account with "
"`QiskitRuntimeService.save_account()`, the client loads your default saved "
"account, and you can skip to [Verify your setup](#verify-your-setup).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have not saved an account, save your API key and instance CRN one "
"time in a trusted environment:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This method writes your credentials to the same file as "
"[`QiskitRuntimeService.save_account()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#save_account). The client uses the "
"`ibm_quantum_platform` channel by default, so you do not need to set "
"`channel`. To save more than one account, set `name`, and pass the same "
"`name` when you create the client.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more options, such as saving several accounts or selecting an instance "
"automatically, see [Save your login credentials](/guides/save-credentials). "
"If you work on a public computer or another untrusted environment, do not "
"save your credentials. Instead, follow [Initialize the service in an "
"untrusted environment](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Verify your setup {#verify-your-setup}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Connect to managed workflows with your saved account, and list the workflows"
" that you uploaded:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have not uploaded a workflow yet, the output is an empty list (`[]`)."
" If you see an authentication error, the client did not find valid "
"credentials. Check the account that you saved in the "
"[Authenticate](#authenticate) section.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow) to upload a workflow, run it, and get its result.\n"
"- To start from working code, deploy one of the [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), or adapt a base template for your own workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
